elliot page is living his truth  in the new cover story for time magazine  the 34 year old actor  opens up for the first time since coming  out as a transgender man  in december 2020 and shares the response  he's received  since sharing his story quote what i was  anticipating was  a lot of support and love and a massive  amount of hatred and transphobia  that's essentially what happened the  umbrella academy star talks about his  childhood and frequent desire to cut his  hair short  saying he struggled with his gender  identity for decades  i felt like a boy i wanted to be a boy i  would ask my mom if i could be someday  just getting to be who i am is such an  incredible experience and i feel  grateful for it  and you know i'm in a very fortunate  place in my life  after his fame grew thanks to films like  juno and  inception paige says he was struggling  with depression  anxiety and panic attacks quote i just  never recognized myself  for a long time i could not even look at  a photo of myself  one decision paige made to help him feel  more comfortable in his  own skin was to undergo top surgery a  procedure to remove one's breast tissue  when he came out as transgender this  past winter  he was recovering from the surgery quote  it has completely transformed my life  i'm incredibly grateful paige adds that  the procedure was not  only life-changing but life-saving he  also opens up about choosing the name  elliot explaining that he always liked  it  especially after the 80s classic e.t  he even has a tattoo that reads ep  phone home a nod to the iconic film and  his initials  e t home  phone e.t phone  and paige says it was the coronavirus  pandemic that led him to coming to terms  with his gender identity  i had a lot of time on my own to really  focus on things that i think  in so many ways unconsciously i was  avoiding  i was finally able to embrace being  transgender  and letting myself fully become who i am  it's a similar sentiment  paige previously shared with et when he  came out as gay  in 2014. i feel so happy  and i feel so different from how i felt  when i was closeted  and while paige is candid about this  part of his life  he did not discuss his divorce from wife  emma portner  who has been publicly supportive of his  decision to transition  he did however share that they separated  last summer and  officially divorced in early 2021 adding  that they've remained  close friends so what's next for paige  he says he's looking forward to  continuing his acting career now that  he's living his truth  quote i'm really excited to act now that  i'm fully who i am  in this body no matter the challenges  and difficult moments of this  nothing amounts to getting to feel how i  feel now  you
 

